  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Rhode Island received $600M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 3,691 awards with an average award size of $162K. Obligations fell 33.8% year over year. The Department of Defense led buying, obligating $490M of the total. Engineering Services is the largest industry by obligations at $220M. Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing accounted for $71.4M, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) accounted for $49.9M. Top vendors included RAYTHEON COMPANY at $80.5M, SEACORP, LLC at $61.8M, and RITE-SOLUTIONS, INC. at $53.5M. Fiscal year comparisons show FY21 at $928M, FY22 at $1.2B, FY23 at $1B, FY24 at $1.2B, FY25 at $906M, and FY26 at $600M. Note that current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date. This snapshot highlights concentration in Defense buying, large engineering services obligations, and a handful of vendors receiving the largest shares of FY2026 to date obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers in Rhode Island?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $490M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs follows at $51.8M, then the Department of Homeland Security at $16.7M and the General Services Administration at $11.3M. Smaller buyers include the Department of Labor at $7.6M and NASA at $6.3M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest contractors and which industries get the most obligations?",
        "body": "RAYTHEON COMPANY is the largest contractor at $80.5M, followed by SEACORP, LLC at $61.8M and RITE-SOLUTIONS, INC. at $53.5M. Engineering Services is the top industry at $220M, with Ammunition (except Small Arms) Manufacturing at $71.4M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $49.9M. Additional notable industries include Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $42.4M and Search, Detection, Navigation, Guidance, Aeronautical, and Nautical System and Instrument Manufacturing at $27.6M."
      }
    ]
